me"],["Red onion","ingredient/red-onion"]]}]},"dish/hasselback-potatoes":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/hasselback-potatoes","n":"Hasselback potatoes","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Swedish cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Hasselback potatoes or Potato à la Hasselbacken are baked potatoes cut about halfway through into thin, fan-like slices. Hasselbacking is done to a fruit or vegetable to create artful-looking food while adding more flavor. This creates a crispy outside while allowing the flavors to penetrate the potato, leaving the inside fluffy. They can be served as a main course, a side dish, or canapé. Various toppings, such as caraway seeds, paprika, cheese, bacon, and breadcrumbs, can be added for extra flavor. Some recipes call for stuffing the toppings between the slices, while others are added closer to the end of the baking process."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-hasselback-potatoes"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hasselback_potatoes"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Swedish cuisine","cuisine/swedish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Breadcrumbs","ingredient/breadcrumbs"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Scandicuisine: Swedish recipes","ref":"site/scandicuisine-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"scandicuisine.com","note":"Traditional Swedish recipes from Cecilia, a cook from a Finnish-Swedish family on Åland.","url":"https://scandicuisine.com/category/swedish-recipes","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Swedish cuisine","links":[["Biff à la Lindström","dish/biff-a-la-lindstrom"],["Blåbärssoppa","dish/blabarssoppa"],["Blodpalt","dish/blodpalt"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Flying Jacob","dish/flying-jacob"],["Fruktsoppa","dish/fruktsoppa"],["Glögg","dish/glogg"],["Isterband","dish/isterband"],["Kebab pizza","dish/kebab-pizza"],["Korv stroganoff","dish/korv-stroganoff